WEBVTT

00:11.136 --> 00:12.053
We're here.

00:12.137 --> 00:12.971
Come down here.

00:13.054 --> 00:14.514
Make sure we have all the tools.

00:14.597 --> 00:16.016
We'll move in right away.

00:16.099 --> 00:17.851
Photograph the scene from all angles.

00:19.978 --> 00:22.397
Check for other bone fragments
once the water drains.

00:23.231 --> 00:26.568
There's no remaining soft tissue,
so the cause of death is unknown.

00:26.651 --> 00:29.362
Still, there are no fractures
or signs of homicide.

00:29.446 --> 00:31.489
Judging by the pelvic bone,

00:31.573 --> 00:35.035
I'd say it's a male
in his twenties or thirties.

00:35.118 --> 00:36.995
- Did you say male?
- Yes.

00:38.538 --> 00:39.956
JOHN DOE

00:40.040 --> 00:41.499
"Twenties or thirties…"

00:43.209 --> 00:44.544
- Kang Ji-hwon.
- Kang.

00:47.630 --> 00:49.466
Hey, there's broken glass here.

00:52.302 --> 00:54.262
Find all possible DNA to compare.

00:54.345 --> 00:55.597
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

01:21.456 --> 01:22.290
Viagra?

01:29.672 --> 01:34.052
Recently, we found a body in the sewers
with its face horribly mutilated.

01:34.552 --> 01:36.179
The victim's name is Sarah Kim.

01:37.097 --> 01:41.226
Due to the lack of defensive wounds,
we think the victim knew her attacker.

01:42.185 --> 01:45.605
FUCK IT. I LOVE YOU
MY LOVE DAMNED IT ALL

01:45.688 --> 01:48.566
The two of you were quite serious,
weren't you?

01:48.650 --> 01:51.236
I believe you have a lot to tell me.

01:53.696 --> 01:56.116
When did you get that scratch
on your hand?

01:57.742 --> 01:58.868
Mr. Kang Ji-hwon.

01:59.786 --> 02:01.663
No secret can stay hidden forever.

02:01.746 --> 02:02.622
I…

02:03.706 --> 02:04.833
I killed her.

02:09.337 --> 02:10.964
One more shot!

02:13.883 --> 02:14.759
Let's do one more.

02:14.843 --> 02:16.719
That's weak!

02:16.803 --> 02:18.805
Come on, let's go!

02:19.722 --> 02:21.391
- Damn.
- Nice.

02:21.474 --> 02:22.934
Eun-jae was my whale.

02:23.434 --> 02:25.728
Wait, not Mok Ga-hui?

02:25.812 --> 02:27.981
No, Kim Eun-jae.

02:28.064 --> 02:29.983
That's Sarah Kim's Korean name.

02:30.608 --> 02:31.442
Hang on.

02:32.694 --> 02:33.695
Mok Ga-hui?

02:35.155 --> 02:37.532
Mok Ga-hui? Is that her real name?

02:37.615 --> 02:39.617
That wasn't her birth name either.

02:40.743 --> 02:43.371
Everything on her résumé was fake.

02:44.622 --> 02:47.584
She cleverly used the fact
that résumés aren't properly checked.

02:48.626 --> 02:49.460
It's likely

02:50.420 --> 02:54.048
she used similar tactics
to get close to you.

02:54.549 --> 02:57.010
No, that wasn't the case.

02:58.136 --> 02:59.929
I approached her first.

03:01.472 --> 03:02.765
Goodness.

03:04.809 --> 03:05.894
We have a new face.

03:07.061 --> 03:07.896
Your name?

03:10.231 --> 03:11.107
Kim Eun-jae.

03:11.608 --> 03:14.402
Nice to meet you. I'm Kang Ji-hwon.

03:14.903 --> 03:17.238
That's "hwon," not "won."

03:19.532 --> 03:23.995
I heard you use the names of people
you really hate as your aliases here.

03:24.621 --> 03:25.705
Is that true?

03:25.788 --> 03:28.374
Where on earth did you hear that?

03:29.542 --> 03:31.336
So, who is Kang Ji-hwon?

03:32.420 --> 03:34.088
I feel bad for the poor guy.

03:35.590 --> 03:36.758
It's my real name.

03:39.844 --> 03:42.347
Allow this "poor guy" to pour you a drink.

03:47.518 --> 03:49.020
I only dealt with married women.

03:49.103 --> 03:54.192
They tend to open their wallets and hearts
more readily than single women.

03:54.275 --> 03:55.944
Wait. Are you saying…

03:56.027 --> 03:56.861
Yes.

03:57.695 --> 03:58.613
Eun-jae

03:59.989 --> 04:00.823
was married.

04:19.968 --> 04:21.511
Are you new to this scene?

04:22.595 --> 04:24.097
It's all a bit awkward, right?

04:28.476 --> 04:30.353
THE ART OF SARAH

04:32.897 --> 04:36.192
KIM EUN-JAE

04:36.276 --> 04:38.069
FOUND YOUR CAR KEYS
CALL ME. JI-HWON

04:38.152 --> 04:39.988
- Nothing yet?
- I can't even enjoy my cig.

04:40.947 --> 04:42.699
I'm smoking. Why eat here?

04:42.782 --> 04:43.992
- For fuck's sake.
- Damn it!

04:44.075 --> 04:46.035
What's with the attitude, you fucker?

04:47.036 --> 04:48.037
Leave him alone.

04:48.121 --> 04:50.540
He tried hard to con this woman,
but got rejected.

04:53.084 --> 04:54.836
This guy's a total has-been now.

04:54.919 --> 04:56.254
Shut the fuck up!

04:56.337 --> 04:57.171
Don't.

04:57.255 --> 04:58.715
- Damn, what a temper.
- Relax.

04:59.882 --> 05:00.925
Let go.

05:02.885 --> 05:04.345
I NEED YOUR HELP

05:08.016 --> 05:09.559
- What the…
- Damn.

05:21.321 --> 05:22.238
Over here.

05:26.326 --> 05:27.160
Take them off.

05:27.744 --> 05:29.871
What? Here?

05:29.954 --> 05:31.205
Your shoes.

05:34.208 --> 05:35.460
Right, my shoes.

05:36.544 --> 05:38.588
Man, did you come out in a hurry?

05:41.632 --> 05:42.633
Here you go.

05:46.888 --> 05:49.140
Be sure to pay me double
for the off-premises fee.

05:49.223 --> 05:50.433
And if you wanted me for--

05:50.516 --> 05:52.018
- Run.
- Wait, where?

05:53.102 --> 05:55.605
Did you run away from home
just to have tteokbokki?

05:57.190 --> 06:00.193
My husband put me on a strict diet.
I can't eat stuff like this.

06:01.444 --> 06:03.237
What does your husband do?

06:04.489 --> 06:05.782
Do you know Hong Seong-sin?

06:07.492 --> 06:08.326
Hong Seong-sin?

06:09.535 --> 06:12.163
How could I not know that name?

06:12.914 --> 06:16.417
Detective, half the guys in this game
owe that prick money.

06:16.501 --> 06:19.045
And the other half
are still paying him back.

06:19.712 --> 06:20.713
What about you?

06:22.298 --> 06:24.133
How much debt did you have?

06:26.969 --> 06:27.845
Well…

06:29.222 --> 06:31.849
Do I have to share
personal stuff like that?

06:34.602 --> 06:37.814
Why are you even married
to a piece of trash like that?

06:38.773 --> 06:40.358
Has he got something on you?

06:41.109 --> 06:43.236
He's a man who needs no explanation.

06:44.195 --> 06:46.948
And when I'm with him,
I no longer need one either.

06:51.786 --> 06:53.246
Why did you drop honorifics?

06:54.664 --> 06:56.249
You look younger than me.

06:56.791 --> 06:58.000
I was born in '92.

06:58.501 --> 06:59.836
I was born in '86.

07:02.922 --> 07:04.882
Come on. Don't lie.

07:05.383 --> 07:09.637
You can't fool me. I don't know much,
but I never get a woman's age wrong.

07:11.681 --> 07:13.391
What do you know about women?

07:14.267 --> 07:17.311
A woman might take years off,
but she'll never add them.

07:22.316 --> 07:25.194
Do you really think I don't know women?

07:26.612 --> 07:30.241
Did you really call me out at this hour
just to eat tteokbokki?

07:31.075 --> 07:33.536
Maybe you wanted to hook up
with a younger guy?

07:35.413 --> 07:36.831
You sound so cheap.

07:37.373 --> 07:40.168
Acting coy would be a misfit move
in this industry.

07:44.881 --> 07:46.966
You were the only one I could contact.

07:58.436 --> 08:00.062
CONTACTS
HUSBAND, CAR KEYS

08:07.987 --> 08:09.947
Ma'am, please give him the change.

08:10.448 --> 08:12.325
- Where are you going?
- Home.

08:12.909 --> 08:14.243
Like now? Why?

08:15.703 --> 08:17.413
Damn, she's a real misfit.

08:17.497 --> 08:19.790
She does think I'm cheap.
I'm a very classy…

08:19.874 --> 08:20.708
Change, please.

08:21.292 --> 08:22.793
Here you go. Please come again.

08:22.877 --> 08:23.920
Wait for me!

08:24.003 --> 08:24.837
Seriously.

08:36.849 --> 08:37.725
CAR KEYS:
PORK BELLY?

08:39.936 --> 08:42.522
HEADING OUT NOW, ICED AMERICANO?
JUST ARRIVED, I'M HERE

08:55.034 --> 08:56.410
Wanna run away with me?

09:04.085 --> 09:05.461
I'm joking.

09:06.337 --> 09:09.966
I won't ask you for money,
so stay another hour with me.

09:15.471 --> 09:16.472
Take it.

09:18.808 --> 09:19.642
What's this?

09:20.643 --> 09:21.519
Hey, this is…

09:23.896 --> 09:27.024
No, this is way too much
for being a runaway's friend.

09:27.108 --> 09:28.901
Your thoughtfulness is enough.

09:29.402 --> 09:30.611
Just take the watch.

09:31.112 --> 09:33.239
You can exchange it if you want.

09:38.744 --> 09:40.162
- Damn prick.
- Damn it!

09:40.246 --> 09:42.123
Bring the money while I'm asking nicely.

09:53.968 --> 09:55.219
For fuck's sake.

10:02.768 --> 10:04.520
That's when it began.

10:04.604 --> 10:06.188
All I did was pour drinks…

10:06.272 --> 10:07.106
WHALE 3

10:07.189 --> 10:10.484
…but for the first time,
I began to pour my heart into the work.

10:14.238 --> 10:15.072
KIM EUN-JAE

10:15.156 --> 10:17.074
Slow down. Don't eat so fast.

10:17.158 --> 10:18.284
Here.

10:27.627 --> 10:28.586
Wait a minute.

10:30.671 --> 10:31.714
What is all this?

10:32.840 --> 10:34.634
- It's nothing.
- No, wait. Are you…

10:35.217 --> 10:36.886
I had enough junkies around me…

10:36.969 --> 10:37.803
Hey, this is…

10:37.887 --> 10:39.221
…to know what they were.

10:39.305 --> 10:42.433
They were track marks.

10:43.851 --> 10:45.561
And those bruises on her

10:46.312 --> 10:47.730
pulled the trigger.

10:48.230 --> 10:49.315
It was him, wasn't it?

10:50.775 --> 10:53.486
Is that fucker making you shoot up,
on top of everything?

10:54.612 --> 10:57.657
- It's not like that.
- Don't give me that crap. This is…

10:58.491 --> 11:02.078
How can you even eat right now?

11:02.787 --> 11:04.330
Why do you live like this?

11:04.997 --> 11:06.332
Are you a fucking idiot?

11:07.500 --> 11:08.501
And that fucker?

11:23.683 --> 11:25.017
Want me to kill him for you?

11:31.607 --> 11:32.441
What?

11:32.525 --> 11:33.818
That fucker…

11:35.820 --> 11:37.571
I really am gonna kill him.

11:57.299 --> 11:58.300
KIM EUN-JAE:
NOW

11:58.384 --> 12:01.429
With him dead,
Eun-jae would inherit his entire fortune.

12:01.512 --> 12:02.346
I thought…

12:04.223 --> 12:08.102
that was the only way
for everyone to be happy.

12:14.608 --> 12:17.403
Is that when you killed Hong Seong-sin?

12:17.486 --> 12:18.320
No.

12:19.530 --> 12:20.740
I couldn't kill him.

12:27.997 --> 12:29.707
Run.

12:38.466 --> 12:40.634
Eun-jae!

12:44.138 --> 12:46.265
Careful now.

12:47.308 --> 12:48.392
Here we are.

13:05.743 --> 13:08.329
I thought I had run far away,

13:09.747 --> 13:11.582
but I realized I had gone nowhere.

13:13.459 --> 13:15.836
I thought the first snow had arrived,

13:17.213 --> 13:18.464
but it was Eun-jae.

13:20.966 --> 13:23.093
I NEED YOUR HELP

13:23.177 --> 13:27.097
Eun-jae had changed a lot
in just a few years,

13:28.891 --> 13:33.062
from the way she dressed and spoke
to her personality.

13:33.646 --> 13:37.191
She even had a different name.

13:37.274 --> 13:38.400
Sarah Kim.

13:39.276 --> 13:40.903
After what happened,

13:40.986 --> 13:43.989
she said she ran like hell
as soon as she came to.

13:44.073 --> 13:48.160
She said she was using an English name
to keep her husband from finding her

13:48.661 --> 13:50.996
and was going to start a whole new life.

13:51.956 --> 13:54.041
She told me
that once Boudoir got established,

13:54.750 --> 13:57.253
she wanted me to manage one of its stores.

13:58.546 --> 14:00.673
So she asked me
to help get it established.

14:02.216 --> 14:04.969
At the time, the person
Eun-jae asked me to entertain was…

14:05.052 --> 14:07.429
- Choi Chae-u.
- You believed those empty words?

14:08.931 --> 14:11.809
- You really expect me to believe that?
- Look.

14:12.476 --> 14:14.520
I had no choice but to believe her.

14:16.313 --> 14:17.314
You see, we had…

14:20.818 --> 14:22.903
promised to have a future together.

14:25.447 --> 14:26.740
Nice house.

14:28.075 --> 14:29.743
Or maybe it's nice to have money.

14:30.619 --> 14:32.997
I'm glad you like it.

14:35.416 --> 14:36.750
Take it. It's a gift.

14:38.752 --> 14:39.587
Okay.

14:40.296 --> 14:41.422
I'll visit often.

14:43.966 --> 14:45.467
The house, not the key.

14:46.051 --> 14:48.721
- I put the contract in your name.
- What?

14:49.763 --> 14:50.723
You did what?

14:52.349 --> 14:55.644
Let's start fresh
and forget all about the past.

14:58.063 --> 15:01.025
They say this place gets so sunny
you don't need an alarm.

15:01.734 --> 15:05.613
We can now sleep at night and wake up
in the morning like everyone else.

15:08.574 --> 15:09.950
Why are you so quiet?

15:14.371 --> 15:15.205
Listen.

15:17.458 --> 15:18.626
Hold on.

15:30.679 --> 15:33.432
About those car keys back then…

15:35.059 --> 15:38.103
Actually, I stole them.

15:40.564 --> 15:41.523
I know.

15:42.399 --> 15:44.109
You knew?

15:49.406 --> 15:53.577
I guess even prestigious Oxford
doesn't teach you to watch out for men.

15:53.661 --> 15:57.456
I mean, after Hong Seong-sin,
you had to choose me of all people.

16:00.042 --> 16:01.835
People are so strange.

16:02.836 --> 16:06.382
They claim that love transcends
status, borders, age, and gender,

16:07.341 --> 16:10.719
but if you fall in love like that,
they'll say it isn't real.

16:17.059 --> 16:19.228
I'm ready to handle anything.

16:21.480 --> 16:22.523
What about you?

16:33.575 --> 16:34.618
Yes, me too.

16:35.619 --> 16:36.829
Whatever it takes.

16:37.329 --> 16:39.039
I can do anything you say.

16:39.790 --> 16:41.208
What can I do to help?

16:52.094 --> 16:55.472
Do you know where people lie the most?

16:57.224 --> 16:58.142
In bed.

17:05.607 --> 17:08.402
I thought you were going to quit smoking.

17:08.986 --> 17:10.988
The cessation pills don't agree with me.

17:12.239 --> 17:13.073
Oh, right.

17:13.657 --> 17:15.576
Chairwoman Shin of GL picked me.

17:15.659 --> 17:18.078
She wants me to come
to Seongbuk-dong tomorrow.

17:20.622 --> 17:21.498
So?

17:22.791 --> 17:23.792
So…

17:25.878 --> 17:27.254
I told her I quit.

17:28.464 --> 17:31.592
You're responsible, you know.
I was forced into unemployment.

17:34.970 --> 17:38.140
I'll get you a position at the office.
Start coming in soon.

17:47.900 --> 17:50.402
Thank you for visiting our humble store.

17:52.071 --> 17:52.905
Oh my God!

17:52.988 --> 17:54.239
Everyone out!

17:54.323 --> 17:55.824
- Now.
- Everyone leave. Now!

17:55.908 --> 17:56.825
You too.

18:02.581 --> 18:03.749
Thank you, Chairwoman.

18:12.299 --> 18:13.175
You know what?

18:14.176 --> 18:15.677
I've never seen the sun once

18:17.262 --> 18:19.306
in all the time I've lived here.

18:19.389 --> 18:21.517
A cold snap is coming
on the day of the party.

18:23.060 --> 18:25.229
I wanted to hold the first part outdoors.

18:31.485 --> 18:32.486
Hey, I…

18:39.326 --> 18:40.577
want to stop.

18:42.955 --> 18:45.415
I'm sick of everything.

18:52.548 --> 18:55.884
Boudoir has really established itself now.

18:57.094 --> 18:58.804
I'm going to tell Choi Chae-u

18:59.721 --> 19:00.806
that I'm quitting.

19:06.395 --> 19:07.813
Who are you to decide that?

19:11.358 --> 19:13.235
- Kim Eun-jae.
- Sarah Kim.

19:14.236 --> 19:15.779
Call me Sarah Kim.

19:53.275 --> 19:58.238
Yes, someone left something at my door.
Could you check the visitor log for me?

19:59.114 --> 20:01.325
- One moment. Apartment 1102, right?
- Yes.

20:02.910 --> 20:05.579
The only visitor on the log today
is Sarah Kim.

20:05.662 --> 20:06.747
Sarah Kim?

20:06.830 --> 20:08.916
Yes, Sarah Kim.

21:37.296 --> 21:39.381
WHALE 2

21:44.177 --> 21:45.178
Hey.

21:46.138 --> 21:47.389
Were you sleeping?

21:48.181 --> 21:50.350
Yes, I wanted to ask you something.

21:50.976 --> 21:54.146
Is your husband the president
of the Oxbridge alumni association?

21:55.272 --> 21:58.233
Then can you look up an alumnus for me?

21:58.317 --> 21:59.526
The name is Sarah Kim.

22:00.485 --> 22:01.403
Born in '86.

22:01.987 --> 22:03.071
That was

22:04.448 --> 22:06.533
a blatant yet subtle threat.

22:07.034 --> 22:09.536
She knew that with me knee-deep
in this mess,

22:11.163 --> 22:13.874
I couldn't report it or do anything.

22:14.374 --> 22:16.501
Why do you think she went to such lengths?

22:17.044 --> 22:19.880
She probably needed me
to lure Choi Chae-u.

22:21.381 --> 22:23.717
If she had even pretended to deceive me,

22:23.800 --> 22:26.178
I would've played along till the end.

22:30.223 --> 22:31.892
Just as I'd pretended to love her…

22:38.648 --> 22:41.068
but ended up actually falling for her.

22:46.656 --> 22:48.450
But she knows that.

22:48.533 --> 22:50.494
She knew how I felt, and she still did it.

22:50.577 --> 22:51.953
Fuck!

22:52.537 --> 22:54.164
How dare you fool me, bitch!

22:54.664 --> 22:58.377
Fuck!

23:11.390 --> 23:12.307
Fuck.

23:13.934 --> 23:15.352
Fuck!

23:22.943 --> 23:23.819
Hong Seong-sin.

23:24.403 --> 23:25.987
Find out his number for me.

23:26.488 --> 23:28.115
Back then, I told Hong Seong-sin

23:29.032 --> 23:31.910
that Eun-jae and I had conspired
to kill him for his money…

23:34.246 --> 23:36.123
and that he'd married a fucking fraud.

23:36.206 --> 23:38.125
I told him everything.

23:40.001 --> 23:41.086
And then,

23:42.629 --> 23:43.672
a few days later,

23:44.548 --> 23:47.759
I saw on the news
that an unidentified body was found

23:47.843 --> 23:48.969
in the sewer.

23:50.262 --> 23:51.888
I knew as soon as I saw it.

23:54.391 --> 23:55.475
"It's Eun-jae."

23:56.935 --> 23:58.270
Are you saying Hong Seong-sin

23:59.646 --> 24:01.314
killed Sarah Kim?

24:01.398 --> 24:02.232
No.

24:03.859 --> 24:05.694
No, I killed her.

24:07.737 --> 24:12.492
I killed Kim Eun-jae and Sarah Kim.
I killed them both!

24:12.993 --> 24:14.494
INTERROGATION IN PROGRESS

24:23.128 --> 24:25.213
I guess it literally was "blind love."

24:25.297 --> 24:26.256
Was it?

24:26.756 --> 24:29.926
He acted exactly like a man
who makes a living calling a con "love."

24:31.011 --> 24:32.888
Didn't you see his eyes earlier?

24:32.971 --> 24:35.182
If that was acting,
then sincerity doesn't exist.

24:35.682 --> 24:38.435
Didn't you notice
he was making statements in his favor?

24:38.518 --> 24:41.354
Kang Ji-hwon is the sole beneficiary
of this scam,

24:41.438 --> 24:42.981
making him at least an accessory.

24:43.064 --> 24:46.067
He's lost too much
to say he has gained financially.

24:46.151 --> 24:47.819
That can't be said for a man

24:47.903 --> 24:50.489
draped head to toe in luxury goods
gifted by whales.

24:51.198 --> 24:54.326
"I only did as I was told.
I was impaired due to intoxication."

24:54.409 --> 24:55.702
"I'm the victim."

24:56.203 --> 24:58.205
All things typically said by criminals.

25:47.629 --> 25:49.548
Thank you.

25:52.008 --> 25:53.218
Thank you.

25:55.887 --> 25:58.431
I was suffering from kidney failure.

26:00.433 --> 26:03.019
I found out
my kidneys were completely shot

26:03.770 --> 26:06.439
only after my kidneys
were completely shot.

26:08.024 --> 26:11.486
The doctors told me
a kidney transplant was my only option.

26:12.612 --> 26:13.613
However,

26:15.115 --> 26:17.450
my siblings from the same mother,

26:18.535 --> 26:20.954
my ex-wife, my estranged children,

26:22.163 --> 26:26.918
and even my lifelong friend of 40 years
all refused to donate a kidney to me.

26:28.378 --> 26:32.090
I was drowning myself in alcohol
like there was no tomorrow.

26:34.801 --> 26:36.386
That's when we met.

26:39.014 --> 26:41.600
I met her when she was working
under the name "Du-a."

26:42.726 --> 26:43.977
Eun-jae, that is.

26:44.978 --> 26:48.857
- I can't stand the sight of you. Get out!
- Hurry up! Come on!

26:54.613 --> 26:55.739
What are you doing?

26:59.200 --> 27:00.201
Well…

27:01.286 --> 27:03.455
It's past our closing time.

27:04.247 --> 27:06.124
I thought you should settle the bill.

27:15.300 --> 27:16.259
Get lost.

27:42.202 --> 27:43.328
Keep it.

27:45.455 --> 27:46.665
Thank you.

27:55.548 --> 27:57.425
Why's a rich man living like this?

28:00.637 --> 28:01.930
I said get lost.

28:05.892 --> 28:07.769
Let me at least make up for the watch.

28:09.854 --> 28:13.692
So I told her about how I had lived
and how I was dying.

28:14.192 --> 28:16.194
I told her everything.

28:18.405 --> 28:21.282
I guess I just wanted
to talk to anyone who would listen.

28:24.035 --> 28:25.870
I'll be your donor.

28:30.417 --> 28:32.085
Give me 500 million won in return.

28:37.716 --> 28:39.551
You want to do an organ trade?

28:41.219 --> 28:43.012
I'm saying we should fake a marriage.

28:46.516 --> 28:47.809
But how can I trust you?

28:51.020 --> 28:52.522
You can pay me afterward.

28:55.608 --> 28:57.360
And just like that,

28:57.444 --> 29:00.321
Du-a jumped headfirst into my dull life,

29:01.072 --> 29:02.907
where I had been only waiting to die.

29:23.511 --> 29:24.971
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD
KIM EUN-JAE

29:27.640 --> 29:28.683
Use that one.

29:29.392 --> 29:34.022
The first thing we did
was give her a new identity.

29:35.398 --> 29:36.441
"Kim Eun-jae."

29:36.524 --> 29:38.526
MARRIAGE REGISTRATION FORM

29:38.610 --> 29:40.487
"Kim Eun-jae." I gave her that name.

29:42.489 --> 29:44.657
That was how we became husband and wife.

29:45.366 --> 29:47.702
That was how we began a marriage

29:47.786 --> 29:52.999
without love, respect,
reverence, truth, duty, or vows.

29:55.126 --> 29:58.838
Since the law required
at least one year of legal marriage

29:58.922 --> 30:01.633
for organ transplants between spouses,

30:01.716 --> 30:04.552
the fake marriage
was intended to last two years.

30:05.261 --> 30:09.641
Our age difference was abnormal
in everyone's eyes,

30:10.141 --> 30:13.770
and even I would've found
the sudden marriage suspicious.

30:17.190 --> 30:18.483
"Oxford"?

30:19.567 --> 30:22.111
If someone asks you about your major,

30:22.821 --> 30:24.906
just say you had your thesis ghostwritten.

30:25.698 --> 30:27.075
Don't clumsily fake it.

30:27.158 --> 30:29.285
That might just rub people the wrong way.

30:29.953 --> 30:31.871
It means I'm stupid and dishonest.

30:32.372 --> 30:34.249
People will look past your ignorance

30:34.332 --> 30:38.211
and only remember your wealth,
which bought you an Oxford degree.

30:38.294 --> 30:41.422
They will be surprised by your frankness
rather than your dishonesty.

30:42.423 --> 30:46.344
"The woman who secured an Oxford degree
by having her thesis ghostwritten."

30:47.095 --> 30:48.263
That one sentence

30:48.346 --> 30:52.475
will engrave you in people's minds
as a genuine, talented, and wealthy woman.

30:58.815 --> 31:02.110
If you know so much,
why don't you manage your reputation?

31:03.903 --> 31:06.573
You're notorious
for being a ruthless loan shark.

31:07.156 --> 31:09.325
Because that is precisely what I want.

31:15.623 --> 31:19.294
Now go shopping for yourself
so you don't look like a bar hostess.

31:24.507 --> 31:25.383
Stay still.

31:25.466 --> 31:27.135
KIM EUN-JAE - F

31:42.400 --> 31:44.402
Press down firmly without rubbing.

31:49.282 --> 31:50.575
When I was young,

31:51.242 --> 31:55.705
a friend used to constantly tease me
about my family's loan business.

31:56.581 --> 32:01.502
One day, that jerk came to see me,
now the CEO of a failing company.

32:01.586 --> 32:03.379
He needed a loan.

32:05.715 --> 32:07.216
What do you think I did?

32:07.800 --> 32:09.177
Did you not lend it to him?

32:09.677 --> 32:13.890
I lent him so much
he could never repay it in his lifetime.

32:16.017 --> 32:20.063
It was enough for him to die,
leaving his son the debt to pay.

32:22.523 --> 32:25.777
One day, the son brought me
that pine tree,

32:26.778 --> 32:29.656
saying he'd dug it up
from his father's grave.

32:29.739 --> 32:32.367
He said it would easily be worth
over 500 million won.

32:34.786 --> 32:36.996
I don't know what got into me at the time,

32:37.664 --> 32:41.584
but I wrote off the rest of his debt
in exchange for that one pine tree.

32:44.253 --> 32:47.256
That was the only act of kindness
I ever showed.

32:47.840 --> 32:48.967
How is that…

32:50.969 --> 32:52.136
an act of kindness?

32:53.763 --> 32:57.392
Because a loan shark gave up
being a loan shark.

33:01.479 --> 33:03.064
I wouldn't have done that.

33:04.315 --> 33:06.567
I'd promise,
but I wouldn't lend them anything.

33:07.568 --> 33:10.530
Then I can get the most painful revenge
without spending a dime.

33:12.156 --> 33:13.825
Because a glimpse of hope

33:14.742 --> 33:17.453
is far more agonizing
than continuous misfortune.

33:18.997 --> 33:20.373
It appears…

33:22.583 --> 33:25.211
you should be the loan shark, not me.

33:40.560 --> 33:42.437
I will repay you double soon.

33:45.690 --> 33:48.151
By the way, why do you look so unwell?

33:48.735 --> 33:51.029
Is your young wife
draining all your energy?

33:51.112 --> 33:52.989
I'm just old too.

33:53.072 --> 33:55.074
You need to come to your senses, Mr. Hong.

33:55.158 --> 33:57.201
Kids these days are very crafty.

33:57.285 --> 34:00.830
I extort money for a living.
Do you think anyone will extort me?

34:02.248 --> 34:04.417
I've already had my will notarized.

34:04.500 --> 34:05.626
Of course.

34:08.212 --> 34:09.380
Excuse me.

34:16.137 --> 34:17.722
I brought some tea.

34:18.973 --> 34:22.143
To appear legitimate and genuine,

34:22.226 --> 34:25.980
we needed a story
that would dispel any doubts about us.

34:29.192 --> 34:31.194
Just do as we practiced.

34:31.944 --> 34:36.282
Today's goal is to make credible people
witness to our relationship.

34:37.825 --> 34:38.659
Understood.

34:38.743 --> 34:41.079
Don't try too hard to impress them.

34:41.621 --> 34:42.955
You'll look desperate.

34:45.416 --> 34:46.793
Do I look desperate?

34:50.296 --> 34:53.424
You're asking me if you seem desperate
with desperation.

34:54.425 --> 34:56.511
Only because you see me that way.

34:59.680 --> 35:02.100
Instead, we build an underwater tunnel

35:02.183 --> 35:05.061
and operate a KTX line
connecting Seoul and Jeju.

35:05.895 --> 35:07.396
But will the airport authorities…

35:07.480 --> 35:10.149
Not a single person there

35:10.233 --> 35:13.069
questioned Eun-jae's background
and origins.

35:15.363 --> 35:17.573
- Wow!
- When will you break ground?

35:19.325 --> 35:20.159
All right.

35:26.541 --> 35:28.417
I think that man is a con artist.

35:30.211 --> 35:32.797
Last time, he said he was an equestrian.

35:32.880 --> 35:35.174
Today, he says
he has swum across the Korea Strait.

35:36.467 --> 35:38.928
I bet next time,
he'll say he was an expert shooter.

35:41.764 --> 35:42.723
Actually,

35:43.224 --> 35:45.601
I saw you lend him
a large sum of money last time.

35:46.352 --> 35:48.479
Maybe you should run
a proper background check.

35:48.563 --> 35:49.772
You think so?

35:55.528 --> 35:58.364
A businessman is not so different
to a con artist.

35:58.865 --> 36:04.036
But there is one thing
that sets him apart.

36:05.246 --> 36:06.372
Do you know what?

36:08.124 --> 36:11.419
He may begin with a bluff,
but he never ends with one.

36:40.114 --> 36:41.490
What are you doing?

36:41.574 --> 36:44.035
You need to undergo dialysis
every six hours.

36:44.785 --> 36:47.622
I know you hate appearing weak,

36:48.164 --> 36:49.957
but don't do that with me too.

36:52.043 --> 36:54.378
- Your buttons. Let me--
- I'll do it. Get out!

36:57.548 --> 36:59.175
You're trembling.

37:12.230 --> 37:14.190
Before I knew it, Eun-jae had become

37:14.690 --> 37:18.527
someone who knew me better
than I knew myself.

37:24.700 --> 37:26.077
Earlier at the party,

37:27.745 --> 37:30.539
what did you say
to make everyone laugh like that?

37:31.666 --> 37:32.750
My husband's flaws.

37:37.797 --> 37:39.215
It seems you had fun.

37:44.136 --> 37:45.137
It made me sad…

37:48.224 --> 37:49.767
because it was all fake.

37:53.437 --> 37:54.897
Well, not everything.

37:57.024 --> 37:59.568
You know your real self comes out

38:01.320 --> 38:03.322
when you let your guard down, right?

38:04.282 --> 38:07.994
And you seem even less aware
that people like that side of you more.

38:10.246 --> 38:11.706
That's the problem.

38:13.874 --> 38:18.004
Even I'm starting to feel confused
about where the lies end…

38:20.881 --> 38:22.466
and the truth begins.

38:27.263 --> 38:28.347
Do you regret it?

38:30.057 --> 38:32.226
Living with you made me realize

38:33.311 --> 38:35.813
that wealth is not a state of being
but a feeling.

38:39.442 --> 38:40.735
It would've been better…

38:43.654 --> 38:46.032
if I had never experienced this feeling.

39:01.047 --> 39:01.881
Eun-jae.

39:07.261 --> 39:09.472
Eun-jae!

39:15.895 --> 39:18.439
I'll call an ambulance. Hang in there.

39:20.107 --> 39:21.984
Did you ask me if I regret it?

39:24.028 --> 39:24.862
I don't.

39:27.782 --> 39:29.158
What should I do?

39:31.494 --> 39:35.039
I think I want to keep living
as Kim Eun-jae.

39:42.213 --> 39:44.548
Eun-jae!

39:52.223 --> 39:53.599
How are you feeling?

39:55.684 --> 39:57.478
Are my kidneys okay?

39:57.561 --> 40:02.441
Do you know the first thing Eun-jae said
when she regained consciousness?

40:02.983 --> 40:05.736
Are my kidneys okay?

40:11.450 --> 40:13.702
Keep the funeral simple.

40:15.204 --> 40:17.873
Cremate the body
and scatter the ashes in my hometown.

40:18.916 --> 40:20.126
And lastly,

40:20.835 --> 40:22.711
I bequeath my entire fortune…

40:24.755 --> 40:27.133
to my wife, Kim Eun-jae.

40:34.932 --> 40:37.435
Your staff is outside.

40:40.479 --> 40:44.275
They've been waiting a while
to greet you in person.

40:45.443 --> 40:48.404
I'm just going to drop by the house
and bring some things too.

40:51.991 --> 40:53.451
Get someone to do it.

40:55.077 --> 40:57.329
I'm feeling stuffy
just being in the hospital.

40:58.873 --> 40:59.915
I'll be back soon.

41:02.501 --> 41:03.502
Okay.

41:21.937 --> 41:24.815
Okay, relax. That's a good girl.

41:26.066 --> 41:27.359
What are you waiting for?

41:27.860 --> 41:29.403
Hurry up. Go make some money.

41:29.487 --> 41:34.158
The day before the operation,
I found out who Eun-jae really was.

41:34.241 --> 41:39.455
She had ended up working at a hostess bar
because she owed money to loan sharks.

41:39.538 --> 41:40.998
CHAIRMAN HONG SEONG-SIN

41:41.081 --> 41:44.919
And that they work for a place I run
called The One Capital.

41:45.002 --> 41:49.298
She was a bitch who borrowed money
from The One Capital about two years ago.

41:50.174 --> 41:53.177
We went to some department store
to press her for the money once,

41:53.719 --> 41:56.805
but we couldn't reach her after that.
Only to turn up here.

41:59.391 --> 42:01.060
She never came by the house.

42:02.311 --> 42:04.104
Looks like the bitch ran already.

42:05.773 --> 42:08.108
I'd promise,
but I wouldn't lend them anything.

42:09.193 --> 42:12.321
Then I can get the most painful revenge
without spending a dime.

42:14.281 --> 42:15.991
Because a glimpse of hope

42:16.909 --> 42:19.662
is far more agonizing
than continuous misfortune.

42:41.809 --> 42:43.435
CHAIRMAN

42:48.816 --> 42:50.317
What happened?

42:50.901 --> 42:52.069
We got her.

42:52.570 --> 42:55.489
It appears she's been planning
to stow away on a boat for months.

42:57.074 --> 42:59.118
She intentionally got close to you

42:59.201 --> 43:01.120
to con you from the very start.

43:03.747 --> 43:05.082
Let her go.

43:06.166 --> 43:07.001
Sir?

43:09.003 --> 43:11.922
I haven't lost anything.

43:14.049 --> 43:16.719
I was the one who had agreed
to be fooled from the start…

43:18.971 --> 43:20.598
so how is that a con?

43:43.912 --> 43:47.041
They say you change
when it's time for you to die.

43:47.541 --> 43:50.711
I started to think
this was karma coming back to me.

44:10.606 --> 44:11.690
Why?

44:13.901 --> 44:15.027
You're awake.

44:16.070 --> 44:18.405
Why did you give me the transplant?

44:19.698 --> 44:21.909
If you had left me to die…

44:25.579 --> 44:28.457
you could've had the entire fortune
to yourself.

44:29.958 --> 44:31.752
I'll just wait a bit longer and get it.

44:33.170 --> 44:35.714
It doesn't seem
like I'll have to wait long.

44:38.926 --> 44:41.011
I wonder
if Eun-jae felt the same way I did.

44:42.596 --> 44:43.681
I can't say for sure.

44:43.764 --> 44:45.349
Go back to sleep. I'll just finish…

44:45.432 --> 44:47.309
I'm certain about one thing.

44:48.018 --> 44:53.023
For that moment, at least,
the con artist gave up being a con artist.

44:53.816 --> 44:57.653
KIM EUN-JAE

44:57.736 --> 45:03.075
And then she vanished,
like she never existed in the first place.

45:12.751 --> 45:16.088
Along with a pine tree
worth 500 million won.

45:16.171 --> 45:19.258
I'll call the landscaping company
and have it restored by today.

45:23.429 --> 45:25.139
No, let's leave it this way.

45:25.222 --> 45:27.349
Did she really
go through with the transplant?

45:30.686 --> 45:33.856
If not, how else would I still be alive?

45:39.528 --> 45:40.529
MEDICAL RECORDS

45:42.698 --> 45:43.782
ORGAN DONATION CONSENT

45:43.866 --> 45:45.993
DONOR - KIM EUN-JAE
RECIPIENT - HONG SEONG-SIN

45:52.249 --> 45:53.292
There weren't any.

45:53.792 --> 45:56.003
There were no signs of surgery
on the body.

45:58.714 --> 46:00.299
Sarah Kim is alive.

46:07.473 --> 46:10.142
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY
PRESS CONFERENCE

46:12.102 --> 46:14.980
This is Park Mu-gyeong
of the Seoul Violent Crimes Unit.

46:15.063 --> 46:17.191
We will now begin the press conference.

46:17.983 --> 46:19.985
Over the years, the suspect has changed

46:20.068 --> 46:22.321
her name, age,
nationality, job, and education,

46:22.404 --> 46:24.823
living under
at least three false identities.

46:25.866 --> 46:26.909
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE

46:26.992 --> 46:29.578
Due to the crime's severity,
a public wanted notice has been issued.

46:29.661 --> 46:32.539
- It is to be effective immediately.
- The one choice

46:32.623 --> 46:36.585
- If you have any information, we urge you.
- It will change your life

46:36.668 --> 46:38.712
Please contact
the Seoul Violent Crimes Unit.

46:38.796 --> 46:40.631
The one choice

46:44.384 --> 46:47.137
Do you know when we find people
who vanish voluntarily?

46:52.518 --> 46:54.144
When they decide to return.

48:19.938 --> 48:24.943
Subtitle translation by: Yung Un Choi
